{"kind":"assert","text":"E5 timeout ruling: no production split for the harness. Section 7.4 asks for one behavior, the wait. Production code must not keep an immediate-return path only because a test scheduler awaits each request synchronously. That would test a path members never run, and leave the waits members do run untested at scale.\n\nChange the test boundary instead. When a generated step's submit waits on sources, the scheduler keeps that call pending. It goes on to deliver the earlier entry or advance the fake clocks, then awaits the call and checks the invariants after it settles. A step whose wait can never resolve in its script is a finding, not a pass. Keep the 400 seeds, the 80 steps, every existing assertion and the 600-second deadline. Invariant 6 also checks the new unsigned-authorization rows.\n\nOne exception needs a report first. If a production caller outside the test needs the C3 selector's immediate source return, for example a caller that the note documents, name that caller and the section before you keep two paths. The repaired head gets one new full gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}